// =============================================================================
// Detection: Security info (MFA / passwordless method) registered from an
//            unfamiliar or risky context
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform  (lab/ - ITDR pack)
// SPL twin:  lab/splunk/detections/security-info-registered-risky.spl
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   A user registering their OWN authentication method (Authenticator, phone,
//   passkey ...) where the sign-in around it looks wrong: risky, from a
//   country the user has not signed in from in the last 14 days, or from an
//   unmanaged device. This is the persistence step after a password or
//   session is stolen (or after a social-engineered help-desk TAP, MGM 2023 /
//   CISA AA23-320A): the attacker adds a method THEY own, and every later
//   sign-in is "MFA satisfied". The admin-on-behalf version of the same move
//   is auth-method-changed-by-admin.kql; this is the self-service half.
//   The preventive control is a CA policy on the "Register security
//   information" user action (passwordless-rollout-plan.md, "Not built");
//   this rule watches the same moment from the log side.
//     "User registered security info"                -> one method added
//     "User registered all required security info"   -> interrupt-mode
//                                                       registration finished
//   The context sign-in is the user's successful sign-in - interactive OR
//   non-interactive - in the hour before the registration (up to 5 min
//   after), preferring the one from the same IP the audit record names.
//   Non-interactive matters: the classic persistence move after token theft
//   is to replay a stolen refresh/session token (logged only in
//   AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs) and then register an authenticator.
//   A registration with NO context sign-in at all (NoContext) is itself
//   surfaced at Medium, never dropped.
//
// SEVERITY (dynamic - the Severity column)
//   High   : the user is privileged or PIM-eligible (PrivilegedUserIds, else
//            the naming convention) - every registration, risky or
//            not, because admin methods are issued in person (help-desk runbook
//            level V3) and must match that ticket; OR sign-in risk high; OR
//            two or more of RiskySignIn / NewCountry / UnmanagedDevice.
//   Medium : exactly one of RiskySignIn / NewCountry (UnmanagedDevice alone
//            never alerts: most staff devices are not compliant yet); OR no
//            context sign-in in either table (NoContext).
//   (No row for a non-privileged registration with no risky signal.)
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   AuditLogs (Category UserManagement; Microsoft lists the service as
//   "Authentication Methods") + SigninLogs and
//   AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs (context) + SigninLogs (14-day country
//   baseline). Activity names: Microsoft Learn's combined-registration
//   troubleshooting table spells them "User registered security
//   information." and "User registered all required security information.",
//   while tenants log "User registered security info" (Microsoft Q&A, 2026-
//   06). The regex accepts both. verify: the exact OperationName, and whether
//   InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress is populated, on the first registration in
//   the lab tenant.
//   DeviceDetail.isCompliant / isManaged and the "Temporary Access Pass"
//   text in AuthenticationDetails: verify on the first TAP sign-in.
//
// LICENSE
//   AuditLogs and sign-in logs: Free per Learn's monitoring-and-health
//   licensing table (verify: Free tenants can route SignInLogs and
//   AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs through diagnostic settings - see
//   modules/entra-diagnostics main.tf LICENSING). Sign-in risk needs P2 (else
//   "hidden" - RiskySignIn never fires, NewCountry still does).
//
// MITRE ATT&CK
//   T1098.005 Account Manipulation: Device Registration (Persistence,
//     PrivilegeEscalation)
//   T1556.006 Modify Authentication Process: Multi-Factor Authentication
//     (CredentialAccess, DefenseEvasion, Persistence)
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Travel: a real user adding a method abroad (NewCountry, Medium).
//     Confirm with the user out of band, never by replying to the alert.
//   - Joiners: a new hire registering with the joiner TAP has no 14-day
//     baseline, so NewCountry cannot fire (NoBaseline = true in the output).
//     Privileged joiners still alert High - match them to the V3 ticket.
//   - Passwordless rollout waves (passwordless-rollout-plan.md) produce
//     bursts of privileged registrations. They are expected High rows;
//     close them against the rollout ticket, do not mute the rule.
//   - NoContext (Medium): a sign-in ingested late or older than the 1-hour
//     window. Check both sign-in tables for the user around RegTime; a
//     registration nobody can tie to a sign-in is the token-replay pattern.
//
// TUNABLE
//   LookBack 1h (the rule runs hourly; a record ingested more than an hour
//   late is missed - widen LookBack and rely on incident grouping if that
//   shows up). Baseline 14d (Sentinel's maximum look-back), BaselineGap 2h
//   (the current session never counts as familiar), ContextWindow 1h.
//   Privileged = object id in PrivilegedUserIds (Terraform-rendered, as in
//   auth-method-changed-by-admin.kql) OR bg-admin-NN / tier0-admin-NN.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   Frequency 1h · Lookback 14d (the country baseline) · one alert per row ·
//   Severity column · Entities: Account = UserPrincipalName / UserId,
//   IP = IPAddress (context sign-in IP, else the audit record's). Sentinel
//   only: Log Analytics alerts cannot look back 14 d.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE
//   Notify on every incident; containment card on High (the USER: revoke
//   sessions). Deleting the new method is a manual step (Entra admin center
//   > user > Authentication methods), after the user confirms it is not
//   theirs - deleting a clinician's only key mid-shift locks them out.
// =============================================================================

let LookBack      = 1h;
let Baseline      = 14d;
let BaselineGap   = 2h;
let ContextWindow = 1h;
let Grace         = 5m;
// Privileged users by OBJECT ID (rendered by modules/monitoring, as in
// auth-method-changed-by-admin.kql; committed empty, so a standalone run falls
// back to naming only).
let PrivilegedUserIds = dynamic(["11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"]); // @@PRIVILEGED_USER_IDS@@
let Registrations = AuditLogs
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack)
    | where Category =~ "UserManagement"
    | where Result =~ "success"
    | where OperationName matches regex @"(?i)^User registered (all required )?security info(rmation)?\.?$"
    // Self-service: the user is the actor. The User target is the fallback.
    | mv-apply tr = TargetResources on (
        summarize TargetId  = take_anyif(tostring(tr.id), tostring(tr.type) =~ "User"),
                  TargetUpn = take_anyif(tostring(tr.userPrincipalName), tostring(tr.type) =~ "User")
      )
    | extend UserId            = coalesce(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id), TargetId)
    | extend UserPrincipalName = tolower(coalesce(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName), TargetUpn))
    | extend RegIp             = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress)
    | extend Method            = extract(@"(?i)registered (.+?) (?:authentication )?method", 1, ResultReason)
    | project RegTime = TimeGenerated, UserId, UserPrincipalName, RegIp, OperationName, ResultReason,
              Method, CorrelationId,
              RegKey = strcat(UserId, "|", tostring(TimeGenerated), "|", CorrelationId);
// SCHEMA TRAP (as in device-code-signin.kql): LocationDetails and
// DeviceDetail are dynamic in SigninLogs but string in the non-interactive
// table, so each leg projects the same names and types before the union.
let SignIns = union
    (SigninLogs
        | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack + ContextWindow)
        | where ResultType == "0"
        | project SignInTime = TimeGenerated, UserId, SignInIp = IPAddress, SignInType = "interactive",
                  Country = tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion),
                  SignInRisk = RiskLevelDuringSignIn,
                  RiskEvents = tostring(RiskEventTypes_V2),
                  Managed = tostring(DeviceDetail.isCompliant) =~ "true" or tostring(DeviceDetail.isManaged) =~ "true",
                  ViaTap = tostring(AuthenticationDetails) has "Temporary Access Pass",
                  SignInApp = AppDisplayName),
    (AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
        | where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack + ContextWindow)
        | where ResultType == "0"
        | extend Dev = todynamic(tostring(DeviceDetail))
        | project SignInTime = TimeGenerated, UserId, SignInIp = IPAddress, SignInType = "non-interactive",
                  Country = tostring(todynamic(tostring(LocationDetails)).countryOrRegion),
                  SignInRisk = RiskLevelDuringSignIn,
                  RiskEvents = tostring(RiskEventTypes_V2),
                  Managed = tostring(Dev.isCompliant) =~ "true" or tostring(Dev.isManaged) =~ "true",
                  ViaTap = tostring(AuthenticationDetails) has "Temporary Access Pass",
                  SignInApp = AppDisplayName);
// The best context sign-in per registration: in the window, same IP first,
// then the latest. Score = 1,000,000 for an IP match + seconds into the window.
let Context = Registrations
    | join kind=inner SignIns on UserId
    | where SignInTime between ((RegTime - ContextWindow) .. (RegTime + Grace))
    | extend Score = iff(isnotempty(RegIp) and SignInIp == RegIp, 1000000, 0)
                     + datetime_diff('second', SignInTime, RegTime - ContextWindow)
    | summarize arg_max(Score, SignInTime, SignInIp, SignInType, Country, SignInRisk, RiskEvents, Managed, ViaTap,
                        SignInApp)
                by RegKey;
let CountryBaseline = SigninLogs
    | where TimeGenerated between (ago(Baseline) .. ago(BaselineGap))
    | where ResultType == "0"
    | summarize KnownCountries = make_set(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion), 50),
                BaselineSignIns = count()
                by UserId;
Registrations
| join kind=leftouter Context on RegKey
| join kind=leftouter CountryBaseline on UserId
| extend NoContext  = isnull(SignInTime)
| extend NoBaseline = isnull(BaselineSignIns) or BaselineSignIns == 0
// coalesce(..., false): a registration with no context sign-in has null
// context columns, and a null must not leak into Signals.
| extend RiskySignIn = coalesce(SignInRisk in~ ("medium", "high")
                                or RiskEvents has_any ("anonymizedIPAddress", "maliciousIPAddress",
                                                       "suspiciousIPAddress", "unfamiliarFeatures"), false)
| extend NewCountry = coalesce(not(NoBaseline) and isnotempty(Country)
                               and not(set_has_element(KnownCountries, Country)), false)
| extend UnmanagedDevice = coalesce(not(NoContext) and not(Managed), false)
| extend PrivilegedById   = isnotempty(UserId) and UserId in (PrivilegedUserIds)
| extend PrivilegedByName = UserPrincipalName matches regex @"(?i)^(bg-admin-[0-9]{2}|tier0-admin-[0-9]{2})@"
| extend PrivilegedTarget = PrivilegedById or PrivilegedByName
| extend Signals = toint(RiskySignIn) + toint(NewCountry) + toint(UnmanagedDevice)
// NoContext: no sign-in in either table explains the registration - surfaced,
// not hidden (a replayed token outside the window, or a log gap).
| where PrivilegedTarget or RiskySignIn or NewCountry or NoContext
| extend Severity = case(
    PrivilegedTarget,     "High",
    SignInRisk =~ "high", "High",
    Signals >= 2,         "High",
    "Medium")
| project TimeGenerated = RegTime, Severity, UserPrincipalName, UserId, PrivilegedTarget, PrivilegedById,
          OperationName, Method, ResultReason, RiskySignIn, SignInRisk, RiskEvents, NewCountry, Country,
          KnownCountries, UnmanagedDevice, ViaTap, NoContext, NoBaseline, Signals, ContextSignInType = SignInType,
          IPAddress = coalesce(SignInIp, RegIp), RegIp, SignInIp, SignInTime, SignInApp, CorrelationId
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
